    "created_at": "2024-12-06T17:45:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-06T17:45:52Z",
    "body": "It looks like Firefox is only sniffing because [our Blob channel inherits from a base channel implementation that sniffs](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/query/default?q=calls-between-source%3A%27mozilla%3A%3Adom%3A%3ABlobURLChannel%27+calls-between-target%3A%27NS_SniffContent%27+depth%3A8) rather than an explicit rationale.  (Whereas our [http channel uses seem much more intentional](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/query/default?q=calls-between-source%3A%27mozilla%3A%3Anet%3A%3AnsHttpChannel%27+calls-between-target%3A%27NS_SniffContent%27+depth%3A8).)\r\n\r\nWhich is to say, I'm fine with Firefox not sniffing and just leaving the content type empty or falling back to text/plain or whatever.  @smaug---- probably has a better opinion than me on this.",
